{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983521-how-to-do-cod-space-opera","id":983521,"title":"How to Do: CoD Space Opera","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-07T14:04:30-07:00","id":983521,"title":"How to Do: CoD Space Opera","content":"So here's a crazy thought, something that I'm not sure I'll ever do but that I've thought about off and on for a while:<br /> How would one do a space opera game in the Chronicles setting?<br /> <br /> The simple answer is &quot;the way you do anything&quot; but there's a few questions worth asking about the setting logistics.<br /> <br /> In the old World of Darkness, outer space doesn't even exist. It's just progressively stranger parts of the Umbra - indeed, a quite viable concept is playing Void Engineers as a starship crew. That they run into things that question dogma constantly is part of the experience - there's a reason they're likely the next Technocrat group to secede. The occasional werewolf encounter is all part of the fun.<br /> <br /> In CoD, it's a bit more mysterious as to what's going on past the Lunar Sphere. The only two mentions I know of involve a mention from the 1e Astral Plane book that talks about travelling in spirit to the spirit of other worlds, and mention from the werewolf book about how Luna shields the earth from Void Spirits, at least one of whom is being kept by an idigam. That spirit might be part of a star from distant space.<br /> <br /> I don't know what else I'm missing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T14:33:46-07:00","id":983535,"title":"","content":"Allow me to introduce you to my favorite CofD supplement: <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/87937/Mirrors-Infinite-Macabre\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/...finite-Macabre</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T14:36:45-07:00","id":983537,"title":"","content":"Depends on what we are talking here. Mirrors: Infinite Macabre handled Space Opera, but it's pretty sparse. There is a bit of discussion on it in various threads. I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7015\" data-vbnamecard=\"7015\">Almarck</a> has space ship and/or mech rules, if you want to use those.<br /> <br /> What exactly are you looking for? Chronicles of Darkness IN SPAAAACE (Humanity mostly tries to ignore the supernatural that exists in its shadows)? Revealed, which the supernaturals are semi-in-the-open, and integrated in the future? Re-classified, where each supernatural is its own phenomena or alien group?<br /> <br /> And what's the theme? Raw Heroism in Space? Interplanetary Romance (genre, not relationships)? Weird Space? Horror in the Big Black?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T15:25:23-07:00","id":983562,"title":"","content":"I'll just leave this here:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/87937/Mirrors-Infinite-Macabre\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/...finite-Macabre</a><br /> <br /> <br /> Damn ninjas!<br /> <br /> <br /> Heh....Okay, I got notes for spaceship rules and I think Amercha has tilts and conditions for space events...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I do question. Why is this a mage specific thread? The only mage relevant thing in your post appears to be... old World of Darkness mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T14:48:46-07:00","id":986401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983521-how-to-do-cod-space-opera#post983521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the old World of Darkness, outer space doesn't even exist. It's just progressively stranger parts of the Umbra - indeed, a quite viable concept is playing Void Engineers as a starship crew. That they run into things that question dogma constantly is part of the experience - there's a reason they're likely the next Technocrat group to secede. The occasional werewolf encounter is all part of the fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't entirely accurate.<br /> <br /> The Void Engineers see space as space, and their will (and the billions of Sleepers) forces it to be space, when they journey through it. Now, if a Dreamspeaker or Hermetic were to go out there, it would look like a weird spirit realm.<br /> <br /> And they aren't <i>really</i> likely to secede, they need the Syndicate's money and resources, and the Progenitors' biografts and constructs to help their ships.<br /> <br /> They just take a lot of aid from the Traditions, because when you're fighting Threat Null, you damn well need that help.<br /> <br /> Besides, lycanthropes are perfectly within the parameters of the Technocratic paradigm, that's the problem with them, the extermination isn't done yet, you see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T18:50:23-07:00","id":987043,"title":"","content":"There's a Mirrors product that expands on Space Opera. It's name escapes me. Mind, it's 1e, but if you're interested enough, porting over shouldn't be hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T19:10:09-07:00","id":987053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983521-how-to-do-cod-space-opera?p=987043#post987043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a Mirrors product that expands on Space Opera. It's name escapes me. Mind, it's 1e, but if you're interested enough, porting over shouldn't be hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Infinite Macabre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}